THE REGENT OF SORONG

WEST PAPUA PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF SORONG REGENCY

NUMBER 2 OF 2015

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

THE REGENT OF SORONG,

Considering : a. that violence against women and children is an act that violates the rights and dignity of women and children as human beings;

b. that the implementation of prevention and protection of women and children as victims of violence in Sorong Regency has not been carried out optimally;

c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children from

Acts of Violence;

In view of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 12 of 1969 concerning the Establishment of the Autonomous Province of West Irian and Autonomous Regencies in the Province of West Irian (State Gazette of the Republic

of Indonesia of 1969 Number 47, Supplement to the State

Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2907);

3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia

of 1984 Number 699, Supplement to the State Gazette of the

Republic of Indonesia Number 368);

4. Law Number 10 of 1992 concerning Population Development and Prosperous Family Development

(State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1992

Number 35, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia

Number 3475);

5. Law Number 21 of 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention on Discrimination in Employment and Occupation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1992

Number 57, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia

Number 3836);

6. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

7. Law Number 21 of 2001 concerning Special Autonomy for Papua Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2001 Number 135, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2001 Number 4151) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2008 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2008 concerning Amendment to Law Number 21 of 2001 concerning Special Autonomy for Papua Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 112, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4884);

8. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

9. Law Number 25 of 2004 concerning National Development Planning System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 104, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4421);

10. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, (Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);

11. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587), as amended by Law Number 1 of 2015 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law

Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 24, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5657);

12. Government Regulation Number 79 of 2005 concerning Guidelines for Guidance and Supervision of Regional Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2005 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4593);

13. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 1 of 2014 concerning Formulation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 32);

14. Regional Regulation of West Papua Province Number 11 of 2013 concerning Protection of Women and Children from Acts of Violence (Regional Gazette of West Papua Province of 2013 Number 11, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of West Papua Province Number 79);

With the Mutual Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF SORONG REGENCY and

THE REGENT OF SORONG

DECIDES:

To enact : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE.

text:
Pasal 2

Penyelenggaraan dan Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak dari korban tindakkekerasan dilaksanakan berdasarkan asas :

a. kemanusiaan ;
b. penghormatan terhadap hak-hak korban;
c. keadilan dan kesetaraan gender;
d. pengayoman;
e. non diskriminasi; dan
f. kepentingan terbaik bagi korban.

translated_text:
Article 2

The Implementation and Protection of Women and Children from victims of acts of violence is carried out based on the principles of:

a. humanity;
b. respect for the rights of victims;
c. justice and gender equality;
d. protection;
e. non-discrimination; and
f. the best interests of victims.

text:
Pasal 3

Tujuan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari korban tindak kekerasan untuk : a. mencegah tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak termasuk perdagangan orang;

b. menghapus segala bentuk kekerasan dan diskriminasi terhadap perempuan dan anak ;

c. memberikan rasa aman bagi perempuan dan anak dari korban kekerasan, pelapor, dan saksi;

d. memberikan pelayanan kepada perempuan dan anak dari korban tindak kekerasan;

e. memfasilitasi dan melakukan mediasi terhadap kasus kekerasan dalam rumah tangga untuk mewujudkan keutuhan rumah tangga yang harmonis dan sejahtera; dan

f. pemberdayaan.

translated_text:
Article 3

The objectives of protecting women and children from victims of acts of violence are to: a. prevent acts of violence against women and children including trafficking in persons;

b. eliminate all forms of violence and discrimination against women and children;

c. provide a sense of security for women and children who are victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses;

d. provide services to women and children who are victims of acts of violence;

e. facilitate and mediate cases of domestic violence to realize harmonious and prosperous household integrity; and

f. empowerment.

text:
Pasal 4

Perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan mendapatkan hak-hak sebagai berikut :

a. hak untuk dihormati harkat dan martabat sebagai manusia; b. hak atas pelayanan kesehatan dan psikologis dari penderitaan yang dialami korban;
c. hak atas pendampingan hukum;
d. hak untuk mendapatkan informasi;
e. hak atas penanganan secara rahasia;
f. hak atas rehabilitasi sosial;
g. hak atas penanganan pengaduan;
h. hak korban dan keluarganya untuk mendapatkan kemudahan dalam proses peradilan; dan
i. jaminan atas hak-hak yang berkaitan dengan status sebagai anggota keluarga dan masyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 4

Women and children victims of acts of violence receive the following rights:

a. the right to be respected for dignity and worth as human beings; b. the right to health and psychological services from the suffering experienced by victims;
c. the right to legal assistance;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidential handling;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and
i. guarantee of rights relating to status as family members and society.

text:
Pasal 5

Anak korban tindak kekerasan selain mendapatkan hak-hak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam pasal 4, juga mendapatkan hak-hak khusus sebagai berikut: a. hak atas kelangsungan hidup,tumbuh dan berkembang;

b. hak atas kebutuhan pelayanan dasar;

c. hak perlindungan yang sama; dan

d. hak mendapatkan kebebasan;

translated_text:
Article 5

Child victims of acts of violence in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in article 4, also receive the following special rights: a. the right to survival, growth and development;

b. the right to basic service needs;

c. the right to equal protection; and

d. the right to obtain freedom;

text:
Pasal 6

Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab dalam memberikan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan merupakan tanggung jawab bersama: a. pemerintahan daerah;

b. masyarakat;

c. keluarga;dan

d. orang tua.

translated_text:
Article 6

Obligations and responsibilities in providing protection to women and children from acts of violence are the joint responsibility of: a. regional government;

b. community;

c. family; and

d. parents.

text:
Pasal 7

(1) Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud dalam pasal 6 huruf a, meliputi:

a. menetapkan kebijakan, program, dan kegiatan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
b. melakukan kerja sama dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
c. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana pelaksanaan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan; dan
d. mengalokasikan anggaran penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan sesuai kemampuan keuangan daerah. (2) Tugas Pemerintah Daerah dalam perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan dalam bentuk :
a. Melaksanakan kebijakan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan yang ditetapkan oleh pemerintah;
b. Mengumpulkan data dan informasi tentang perempuan dan anak dalam rangka upaya melindungi dari tindak kekerasan;
c. Melakukan sosialisasi peraturan perundang-undangan yang berkaitan dengan pencegahan dan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan; dan
d. Melakukan pemantauan dan evaluasi penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 7

(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in article 6 letter a, include:

a. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
b. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
c. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence; and
d. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with regional financial capacity. (2) The duties of the Regional Government in protecting women and children from acts of violence in the form of:
a. Implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence established by the government;
b. Collecting data and information about women and children in order to protect them from acts of violence;
c. Conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence; and
d. Conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.

text:
Pasal 11

(1) Pencegahan terjadi tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam pasal 10, dilaksanakan oleh SKPD yang tugas dan fungsinya dibidang:

a. sosial;
b. kesehatan;
c. pendidikan;
d. ketenagakerjaan;
e. pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak;
f. mental dan spiritual; dan
g. ketentraman dan ketertiban.
(2) Pencegahan tindak kekerasan oleh SKPD sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1),dilaksanakan secara terpadu dan berkesinambungan.

translated_text:
Article 11

(1) Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in article 10, is implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the field of:

a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual matters; and
g. peace and order.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), is implemented in an integrated and continuous manner.

text:
Pasal 12

(1) Bentuk pelayanan yang diberikan kepada perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan,sebagai berikut :

a. pelayanan pengaduan;
b. pelayanan medis; dan
c. pelayanan medikolegal untuk kepentingan pembuktian dibidang hukum. (2) Pelayanan bantuan hukum:
a. pelayanan kemandirian atau pemberdayaan; dan
b. pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial.
(3) Bentuk pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), dilaksanakan oleh SKPD terkait sesuai dengan program, kegiatan, dan anggaran yang tersedia di masing-masing dalam bidang:
a. sosial;
b. kesehatan;
c. pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak;
d. mental dan spriritual;
e. ketenagakerjaan; dan
f. pendidikan.

translated_text:
Article 12

(1) Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence, are as follows:

a. complaint services;
b. medical services; and
c. medicolegal services for the purposes of evidence in the field of law. (2) Legal aid services:
a. independence or empowerment services; and
b. social rehabilitation services.
(3) Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), are implemented by relevant SKPD in accordance with the programs, activities, and budget available in each in the field of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection;
d. mental and spiritual matters;
e. manpower; and
f. education.
